# tools/m/mycelium_chorus_bron_witness.rish -- a quorum of vouchers travels as a readable record (r2).
#
# Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) - Mycelium consensus - the Chorus - rung r2 -- travel.
# r1 gathered a Chorus -- a bounded quorum of independent Vouchers for one account position at one
# order-head -- and proved it is believed only when a threshold of distinct nodes agree. A quorum a holder
# cannot hand to another is only a local reading, so r2 lets the whole Chorus cross as `format chorus-v1`
# bytes. Because every member attests the SAME claim, the record names the claim once -- a `head` line, an
# `account` line, a `position <balance> <reserved> <received>` line, a `threshold <t>` line -- then one
# `member <node-hex> <sig-hex>` line per voice. Render writes it, parse reads it back, a round trip a
# fixed point.
#
# The crux this witness proves is THE QUORUM LAW SURVIVES THE WIRE: a parsed Chorus is reconstructed
# member by member from the shared claim, then re-run through r1's verify_chorus at the record's own
# stated threshold -- so a record whose members do not meet that threshold (BelowThreshold), whose members
# are not distinct (DuplicateNode), or one of whose signatures does not verify over the claim
# (BadSignature) refuses before it is trusted. A recipient reads the same quorum r1 asserted, needing no
# ledger of their own; a recipient who DOES hold the blocks can still run r1's check_against on the
# recovered Chorus. A wrong header - unknown field - missing field - bad hex key each refuse. Composes
# chorus.rye + voucher.rye public API only; demo seeds -- no key, no funds, no network, no custody.
#
# Scope: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-102533_mycelium-chorus-quorum-attestation-exploration.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mycelium_chorus_bron_witness.rish

say "mycelium-chorus-bron: Language EN — a whole quorum crosses a wire: the claim named once, each voice adding only its node key and signature, and the recovered quorum proves itself at threshold before anyone trusts it."
say "mycelium-chorus-bron: Style Radiant — r1 made a quorum believable in one place; r2 lets it travel and still prove itself, so a stranger who receives the bytes needs no ledger of their own to check that distinct nodes agreed."
say "mycelium-chorus-bron: Lens TAME — the record is a purpose-built bounded reader over chorus + voucher public API; render and parse round-trip byte-for-byte; the quorum law re-runs on the recovered chorus; a forged member, a thin record, a padded record, and each malformed field refuse; demo seeds only, no key held."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mycelium/bin/chorus-bron"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/chorus_bron.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "mycelium-chorus-bron: build failed"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "mycelium-chorus-bron: selftest exited non-zero"
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: selftest did not speak GREEN"
assert selftest.out contains "parses back byte-for-byte (fixed point)" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: fixed-point claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "proves itself at threshold offline after the crossing" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: proof-survives-wire claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "a forged member refuses BadSignature, a thin record BelowThreshold, a padded record DuplicateNode" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: quorum-refusal claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "a bad header, an unknown field, a missing field, a bad hex key each refuse" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: malformed-refusal claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "voices=3 · fixed point" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: recovered-quorum summary missing"

# The Chorus each record carries stands at the door -- its own r1 selftest proves the quorum law the wire
# re-runs on every recovered record.
let chorus = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/chorus.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/chorus && mycelium/bin/chorus 2>&1"]
assert chorus.ok else "mycelium-chorus-bron: the Chorus the record carries is not GREEN"
assert chorus.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-chorus-bron: the Chorus did not speak its GREEN"

say "mycelium-chorus-bron: GREEN — a quorum of vouchers renders to a format chorus-v1 record and parses back byte-for-byte, proving itself at threshold offline after the crossing and checking against the ledger it vouches; a forged member · a thin record · a padded record · a bad header · an unknown field · a missing field · a bad hex key each refuse; the Chorus r1 stands at the door."
